Description: Patrone Remote Desktop first in System > Remote Desktop
 With patrone-remote-desktop installed, System > Remote Desktop's first
 tab is Patrone's page, named Remote Desktop (panels/system/remote-desktop/
 cc-patrone-remote-login.c, from gnome-settings/remote-login in Patrone's
 repository): a "Remote Desktop" switch, how to connect, and what the
 other ways in do. It takes the place of GNOME's Remote Login, which
 drives gnome-remote-desktop's system daemon; Desktop Sharing comes after
 it, and System's Remote Desktop row says what it's for. Secure Shell's
 row says what SSH does. Without the package, the page is GNOME's.
Author: William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
---
